# optim_bench.py writes `--out tests/benchmarks/optim-baseline/<tag>-pass1.json`
# (warm-up, discarded) and then `<tag>-pass2.json` (measurement, kept) -- the
# protocol in docs/developer/multi-instance-optimization-plan.md. A warm-up is
# never evidence, so it stays out of the tree; a pass2 a doc cites is committed
# normally.
*-pass1.json
